/* The product mark: a tree growing downwards from its root, in the same teal
   the rest of the plugin uses. Compiled by msbuild (an <RcCompile> item in the
   .dproj) and linked by the .dpk.

   ONE BITMAP, TWO USES - the startup splash line
   (PasTreeIdePlugin.Splash.pas) and the settings dialog's header
   (PasTreeIdePlugin.SettingsForm). It is named for the product rather than for
   either of them so that neither reads as owning it, and so a third use needs
   no second copy to drift from this one.

   THE BITMAP IS TRACKED AND THE .res IS NOT: *.res is generated output here
   (see .gitignore), so the source of the image has to be something a build can
   turn into one.

   24x24 IS FIXED BY IOTASplashScreenServices.AddPluginBitmap, which documents
   that size and reads the LOWER-LEFT PIXEL AS THE TRANSPARENT COLOUR. It is
   magenta here, which is why the artwork must never touch that corner - and
   why the image is drawn with antialiasing off, since blended edge pixels are
   not exactly the transparent colour and would show as a halo around every
   shape. VCL's TBitmap.Transparent uses the same bottom-left convention, which
   is what lets the settings dialog show it without a second, masked copy. */
PASTREE_LOGO BITMAP "PasTreeIdePlugin.Logo.bmp"
